From e1a68349eeb637a4b7ce7158b840ed11c0633e04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patrickjquinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:11:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 210/214] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt6858: Add the LVTS sensors
 and thermal zones

The only thermal zone is the battery's, so nothing throttles the CPUs
or the GPU however hot the SoC gets.

Add the MCU and AP LVTS controllers and a zone for the hotter sensor of
each core, for the DSU and for the top and bottom of the SoC. The hotter
sensors were measured with every core loaded: each big core's second
sensor, DSU1, AP top 2 and AP bottom 1. Each zone has:
- polling every 2 s, every 250 ms past a trip;
- a passive trip at 85 degC that throttles the cores' own cluster
  (all CPUs for the DSU; all CPUs and the GPU for the SoC zones);
- a critical trip at 110 degC, below the preloader's 115 degC thermal
  reset, which stays as the preloader armed it.

On the Jolla Phone (2026), through an overlay of these nodes: idle at a
28.5 degC battery the zones read 34-37 degC, and loading the cores
raised them by 9-15 degC. Panthor's devfreq cooling bound to the two
SoC zones.
